ill own the increased collateral position.\",\"data\":\"Arbitrary data to pass to the `onMorphoSupplyCollateral` callback. Pass empty data if not needed.\"}},\"withdrawCollateral((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256,address,address)\":{\"details\":\"`msg.sender` must be authorized to manage `onBehalf`'s positions.Withdrawing an amount corresponding to more collateral than supplied will revert for underflow.\",\"params\":{\"marketParams\":\"The market to withdraw collateral from.\",\"assets\":\"The amount of collateral to withdraw.\",\"onBehalf\":\"The address of the owner of the collateral position.\",\"receiver\":\"The address that will receive the collateral assets.\"}},\"liquidate((address,address,address,address,uint256),address,uint256,uint256,bytes)\":{\"details\":\"Either `seizedAssets` or `repaidShares` should be zero.Seizing more than the collateral balance will underflow and revert without any error message.Repaying more than the borrow balance will underflow and revert without any error message.An attacker can front-run a liquidation with a small repay making the transaction revert for underflow.\",\"params\":{\"marketParams\":\"The market of the position.\",\"borrower\":\"The owner of the position.\",\"seizedAssets\":\"The amount of collateral to seize.\",\"repaidShares\":\"The amount of shares to repay.\",\"data\":\"Arbitrary data to pass to the `onMorphoLiquidate` callback. Pass empty data if not needed.\"},\"returns\":{\"_0\":\"The amount of assets seized.\",\"_1\":\"The amount of assets repaid.\"}},\"flashLoan(address,uint256,bytes)\":{\"details\":\"Flash loans have access to the whole balance of the contract (the liquidity and deposited collateral of allWarning: Not ERC-3156 compliant but compatibility is easily reached:\",\"params\":{\"token\":\"The token to flash loan.\",\"assets\":\"The amount of assets to flash loan.\",\"data\":\"Arbitrary data to pass to the `onMorphoFlashLoan` callback.\"}},\"setAuthorization(address,bool)\":{\"params\":{\"authorized\":\"The authorized address.\",\"newIsAuthorized\":\"The new authorization status.\"}},\"setAuthorizationWithSig((address,address,bool,uint256,uint256),(uint8,bytes32,bytes32))\":{\"details\":\"Warning: Reverts if the signature has already been submitted.The signature is malleable, but it has no impact on the security here.The nonce is passed as argument to be able to revert with a different error message.\",\"params\":{\"authorization\":\"The `Authorization` struct.\",\"signature\":\"The signature.\"}}},\"author\":\"Morpho Labs\",\"stateVariables\":{\"DOMAIN_SEPARATOR\":{\"details\":\"Warning: Every EIP-712 signed message based on this domain separator can be reused on another chain sharing\"},\"owner\":{\"details\":\"It has the power to change the owner.It has the power to set fees on markets and set the fee recipient.It has the power to enable but not disable IRMs and LLTVs.\"},\"feeRecipient\":{\"details\":\"The recipient receives the fees of a given market through a supply position on that market.\"},\"position\":{\"details\":\"Warning: For `feeRecipient`, `supplyShares` does not contain the accrued shares since the last interest\"},\"market\":{\"details\":\"Warning: `totalSupplyAssets` does not contain the accrued interest since the last interest accrual.Warning: `totalBorrowAssets` does not contain the accrued interest since the last interest accrual.Warning: `totalSupplyShares` does not contain the accrued shares by `feeRecipient` since the last interest\"},\"isAuthorized\":{\"details\":\"Anyone is authorized to modify their own positions, regardless of this variable.\"},\"idToMarketParams\":{\"details\":\"This mapping is not used in Morpho. It is there to enable reducing the cost associated to calldata on layer\"}},\"title\":\"Morpho\",\"custom:contact\":\"security@morpho.org\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"DOMAIN_SEPARATOR()\":{\"notice\":\"The EIP-712 domain separator. the same chain id because the domain separator would be the same.\"},\"owner()\":{\"notice\":\"The owner of the contract.\"},\"feeRecipient()\":{\"notice\":\"The fee recipient of all markets.\"},\"position(bytes32,address)\":{\"notice\":\"The state of the position of `user` on the market corresponding to `id`. accrual.\"},\"market(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"The state of the market corresponding to `id`. accrual.\"},\"isIrmEnabled(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Whether the `irm` is enabled.\"},\"isLltvEnabled(uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Whether the `lltv` is enabled.\"},\"isAuthorized(address,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Whether `authorized` is authorized to modify `authorizer`'s position on all markets.\"},\"nonce(address)\":{\"notice\":\"The `authorizer`'s current nonce. Used to prevent replay attacks with EIP-712 signatures.\"},\"idToMarketParams(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"The market params corresponding to `id`. 2s by creating a wrapper contract with functions that take `id` as input instead of `marketParams`.\"},\"setOwner(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Sets `newOwner` as `owner` of the contract.\"},\"enableIrm(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Enables `irm` as a possible IRM for market creation.\"},\"enableLltv(uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Enables `lltv` as a possible LLTV for market creation.\"},\"setFee((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Sets the `newFee` for the given market `marketParams`.\"},\"setFeeRecipient(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Sets `newFeeRecipient` as `feeRecipient` of the fee. ensure that the current recipient receives all due fees, accrue interest manually prior to making any changes.\"},\"createMarket((address,address,address,address,uint256))\":{\"notice\":\"Creates the market `marketParams`. Morpho behaves as expected: - The token should be ERC-20 compliant, except that it can omit return values on `transfer` and `transferFrom`. - The token balance of Morpho should only decrease on `transfer` and `transferFrom`. In particular, tokens with burn functions are not supported. - The token should not re-enter Morpho on `transfer` nor `transferFrom`. - The token balance of the sender (resp. receiver) should decrease (resp. increase) by exactly the given amount on `transfer` and `transferFrom`. In particular, tokens with fees on transfer are not supported. - The IRM should not re-enter Morpho. - The oracle should return a price with the correct scaling. (funds could get stuck): - The token can revert on `transfer` and `transferFrom` for a reason other than an approval or balance issue. - A very high amount of assets (~1e35) supplied or borrowed can make the computation of `toSharesUp` and `toSharesDown` overflow. - The IRM can revert on `borrowRate`. - A very high borrow rate returned by the IRM can make the computation of `interest` in `_accrueInterest` overflow. - The oracle can revert on `price`. Note that this can be used to prevent `borrow`, `withdrawCollateral` and `liquidate` from being used under certain market conditions. - A very high price returned by the oracle can make the computation of `maxBorrow` in `_isHealthy` overflow, or the computation of `assetsRepaid` in `liquidate` overflow. the point where `totalBorrowShares` is very large and borrowing overflows.\"},\"supply((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256,uint256,address,bytes)\":{\"notice\":\"Supplies `assets` or `shares` on behalf of `onBehalf`, optionally calling back the caller's `onMorphoSupply` function with the given `data`. caller is guaranteed to have `assets` tokens pulled from their balance, but the possibility to mint a specific amount of shares is given for full compatibility and precision. Consider using the `assets` parameter to avoid this.\"},\"withdraw((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256,uint256,address,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Withdraws `assets` or `shares` on behalf of `onBehalf` and sends the assets to `receiver`. conversion roundings between shares and assets.\"},\"borrow((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256,uint256,address,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Borrows `assets` or `shares` on behalf of `onBehalf` and sends the assets to `receiver`. caller is guaranteed to borrow `assets` of tokens, but the possibility to mint a specific amount of shares is given for full compatibility and precision. Consider using the `assets` parameter to avoid this.\"},\"repay((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256,uint256,address,bytes)\":{\"notice\":\"Repays `assets` or `shares` on behalf of `onBehalf`, optionally calling back the caller's `onMorphoReplay` function with the given `data`. roundings between shares and assets.\"},\"supplyCollateral((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256,address,bytes)\":{\"notice\":\"Supplies `assets` of collateral on behalf of `onBehalf`, optionally calling back the caller's `onMorphoSupplyCollateral` function with the given `data`.\"},\"withdrawCollateral((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256,address,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Withdraws `assets` of collateral on behalf of `onBehalf` and sends the assets to `receiver`.\"},\"liquidate((address,address,address,address,uint256),address,uint256,uint256,bytes)\":{\"notice\":\"Liquidates the given `repaidShares` of debt asset or seize the given `seizedAssets` of collateral on the given market `marketParams` of the given `borrower`'s position, optionally calling back the caller's `onMorphoLiquidate` function with the given `data`.\"},\"flashLoan(address,uint256,bytes)\":{\"notice\":\"Executes a flash loan. markets combined, plus donations). - `flashFee` is zero. - `maxFlashLoan` is the token's balance of this contract. - The receiver of `assets` is the caller.\"},\"setAuthorization(address,bool)\":{\"notice\":\"Sets the authorization for `authorized` to manage `msg.sender`'s positions.\"},\"setAuthorizationWithSig((address,address,bool,uint256,uint256),(uint8,bytes32,bytes32))\":{\"notice\":\"Sets the authorization for `authorization.authorized` to manage `authorization.authorizer`'s positions.\"},\"accrueInterest((address,address,address,address,uint256))\":{\"notice\":\"Accrues interest for the given market `marketParams`.\"},\"extSloads(bytes32[])\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the data stored on the different `slots`.\"}},\"notice\":\"The Morpho contract.\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"lib/crane/contracts/external/morpho/blue/Morpho.sol\":\"Morpho\"},\"evmVersion\":\"osaka\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":1},\"remappings\":[\"@battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/src/\",\"@crane/=lib/crane/\",\"@matterlabs/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/lib/\",\"@nomicfoundation/=node_modules/@nomicfoundation/\",\"@opengsn/=node_modules/@opengsn/\",\"@openzeppelin/=node_modules/@openzeppelin/\",\"@oz/=lib/crane/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\"@ozu/=lib/crane/contracts/external/openzeppelin-upgradeable/\",\"battlechain-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/lib/battlechain-contracts/\",\"battlechain-lib-mocks/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/test/mocks/\",\"battlechain-lib/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/src/\",\"battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-lib/lib/battlechain-safe-harbor-contracts/\",\"chainlink-ccip/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/vendor/optimism/interop-lib/v0/src/\",\"chainlink-evm/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/lib/chainlink-evm/\",\"chainlink-local/=lib/crane/lib/chainlink-local/src/\",\"clones/=lib/crane/contracts/external/clones-with-immutable-args/\",\"contracts/external/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/=lib/crane/contracts/protocols/launchpads/uniswap/continuous-clearing/\",\"contracts/solady/=lib/crane/contracts/external/solady/\",\"crane/=lib/crane/\",\"createx/=lib/crane/lib/battlechain-